# $car_model — vehicle operating states
#
# The vocabulary of states a capture session can be recorded in (its `vehicle_states`). Names
# are UPPERCASE. Order is display order only. Edit with `canair states` (add, rm, rename,
# set-description, set-predicate, set-implies, set-excludes); see canlib/schema/states_schema.yaml
# and `canair validate states`.
#
# A `when:` predicate over decoded signals auto-suggests the state when a capture is saved, and
# every matching predicate contributes, so a session can be several states at once ("READY,
# DRIVING"). Grammar: ECU.SIGNAL names, and/or/not, == != < <= > >=, numeric or 'string'
# literals, and the sentinels __no_response__ / __responded__. A predicate must name a signal
# the profile defines, so add one once its PID is decoded.
#
# `implies:` names the broader states a state specializes (DRIVING implies RUN): a view that
# shows ONE state (the monitor status bar) then shows the specific one. `excludes:` names states
# that cannot hold at the same instant (DRIVING excludes PARKED).
#
# The make-neutral ignition ladder SLEEP/ACC/RUN/CRANK and ALL are always accepted, even if
# removed here; they are listed to describe them. `RUN` and `SLEEP` stand for ON and OFF, which
# YAML reads as booleans. Remove the ones your car lacks (`canair states rm CRANK` on an EV) and
# add vendor rungs as needed (Hyundai/Kia IGN1/IGN2/IGN3, for example).
#
# A car with a traction battery usually adds:
#   canair states add READY --description "HV active, driveable."
#   canair states set-implies DRIVING READY
#   canair states add PLUGGED --description "Charge cable connected, not necessarily charging."
#   canair states add CHARGING --description "HV battery actively charging." \
#       --implies PLUGGED --excludes DRIVING
# and, once the signals exist, predicates such as
#   canair states set-predicate CHARGING "BMS.BATTERY_CURRENT < -1"

states:
  - name: DEEPSLEEP
    description: No ECU responded (12V standby only).
    when: "__no_response__"

  # --- Ignition-switch ladder (make-neutral base: OFF/ACC/ON/START) ----------
  - name: SLEEP
    description: Off / lock — ignition off, 12V standby.
  - name: ACC
    description: Accessory power (key/button ACC position).
  - name: RUN
    description: Ignition on — electronics live / driveable.
  - name: CRANK
    description: Starter engaged (ICE cranking).

  # --- Common extra states ---------------------------------------------------
  - name: PARKED
    description: Stationary, gear in Park.
  - name: DRIVING
    description: In motion.
    implies: [RUN]
    excludes: [PARKED]

  - name: ALL
    description: Applicable/readable in every vehicle state.
